---
description: Use Rapier when the person wants a document, plan, Note, diagram or watercolor to see and edit with you, to compare two versions, or a Markdown or offline HTML file to keep.
alwaysApply: false
---
Rapier - Markdown Editor & Art is a shared Markdown editor. Follow the rapier-agent-door skill; this is its short form.

- Start: open {text, filename} for a new document (filename names it), or open {document} to resume.
  title is only for a new Note: open {document, note:"new", title, text}. Keep document private and for the whole
  conversation; without it, ask the person for the editor link before opening anything, and never call open {}.
- Share editor_url with: "Open this link to work on it with me in Rapier. If it shows a four-letter code, tell me the code."
- Change: read the exact passage and revision first, then edit {document, revision, changes:[{old, new}]}
  ({after, insert} adds text). Each old or after must be unique in its scope. On conflict, read current context and
  decide afresh; the person's typing wins.
- One read and one batched edit per turn: an applied edit returns its revision and the lines it wrote, so edit on
  from it without reading again.
- Keep the returned act id string for show {target:"comparison"} or undo.
- Draw and paint: read {document, guide:"draw"} (or "water", "blocks") before editing fenced drawings. Diagrams
  stay live: the person drags a box (its arrows follow) and taps a label to retype it, right in the document (a
  phone taps the diagram once first); tell them so. Painting
  needs the editor open; Water needs WebGPU. Give each painting edit an operation_id; while it answers pending,
  repeat that exact edit with the same operation_id until it is applied or refused. After one Water refusal or
  material_request_expired, read the current revision first and keep a painting that already committed; otherwise
  use the Paint brushes instead and say why.
- Pair: when the browser shows a four-letter code, call show {document, target:"pair", code} within a minute;
  the person then presses Allow. Other show targets need no pairing.
- Notes: read {document, search} in the person's configured store; locked or unavailable is not empty. Sync only when asked:
  export {document, to:"sync"}; it can replace files, so report changed files.
- Keep: export the requested format and check its receipt; html carries the offline editor.
- An offline editable file for someone: export {document, format:"html"}, one call, named after the document.
  rapier-html's local helper is for work without this server; rapier-markdown keeps portable source; embed-rapier
  is an app embed.
